  "prefLabel": "Nur 608.01 Definitions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Nur 608.01 Definitions.\n\n(a) “Nurse externship” means a clinical learning program pursuant to RSA 326-B:32, (I)(a), whether paid, for course credit, or uncompensated, that supplements an RN student’s education and training through placement in a health care facility at which the nurse extern performs nursing tasks or activities under supervision.\n\n(b) “Nurse extern preceptor” means an office of professional licensure and certification (OPLC) licensed RN or APRN working at a New Hampshire health care facility that meets the qualifications outlined in Nur 608.05.\n\n(c) “Nurse extern” means a student enrolled in a board approved RN education program who practices in a non-licensed capacity in a New Hampshire health care facility under the supervision of a nurse extern preceptor performing delegated and assigned nursing interventions to implement the plan of care.\n\n(d) “Supervision” means direction by a nurse extern preceptor for the accomplishment of a nursing task or activity, including initial direction and periodic inspection of the actual accomplishment of the task or activity.\n\nSource. #13707, 9-27-23; ss by #14636, eff 8-24-26, EXPIRES: 8-24-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/nur100-800.html"
